    {
      "id": "https://www.strangerfoods.org/recipes/zucchini-noodle-bowl-with-walnut-kale-pesto",
      "url": "https://www.strangerfoods.org/recipes/zucchini-noodle-bowl-with-walnut-kale-pesto",
      "title": "Zucchini noodle bowl with walnut-kale pesto",
      "content_html": "<h1 style=\"text-align:center;font-family:sans-serif;\">Zucchini noodle bowl with walnut-kale pesto</h1>\n        <br>\n        <img src=\"https://www.strangerfoods.org/images/zucchini-noodle-bowl-with-walnut-kale-pesto.webp\" style=\"text-align:center;\"/>\n        <br>\n        <p style=\"font-family:sans-serif;>One of my favorite ways to enjoy fresh zucchini at the height of summer is by turning it into noodles. With the help of a spiralizer or vegetable peeler, it becomes a delicious substitute for traditional pasta. The zucchini can be eaten raw, but if you prefer it cooked, simply saut\u00e9 it in a little oil\u2014just be sure to thoroughly dry the noodles or ribbons beforehand. If you don\u2019t have sun-dried tomatoes, substitute halved cherry tomatoes instead.</p>",
      "image": "https://www.strangerfoods.org/images/zucchini-noodle-bowl-with-walnut-kale-pesto.webp",
      "date_published": "2026-07-31T00:00:00+00:00Z",
      "language": "en"
    },
    {
      "id": "https://www.strangerfoods.org/recipes/homemade-sausage-and-egg-mcmuffin",
      "url": "https://www.strangerfoods.org/recipes/homemade-sausage-and-egg-mcmuffin",
      "title": "Homemade sausage and egg mcmuffin",
      "content_html": "<h1 style=\"text-align:center;font-family:sans-serif;\">Homemade sausage and egg mcmuffin</h1>\n        <br>\n        <img src=\"https://www.strangerfoods.org/images/homemade-sausage-and-egg-mcmuffin.webp\" style=\"text-align:center;\"/>\n        <br>\n        <p style=\"font-family:sans-serif;>Copycat of McDonald's Sausage and Egg McMuffin. The sausage patties are made from scratch and it really does taste similar to the McDonald's Sausage patty - but it tastes pure, like real food should! Great make ahead breakfast - grab and run!</p>",
      "image": "https://www.strangerfoods.org/images/homemade-sausage-and-egg-mcmuffin.webp",
      "date_published": "2026-07-26T00:00:00+00:00Z",
      "language": "en"
    },
    {
      "id": "https://www.strangerfoods.org/recipes/pulled-lamb-shawarma-sandwich",
      "url": "https://www.strangerfoods.org/recipes/pulled-lamb-shawarma-sandwich",
      "title": "Pulled lamb shawarma sandwich",
      "content_html": "<h1 style=\"text-align:center;font-family:sans-serif;\">Pulled lamb shawarma sandwich</h1>\n        <br>\n        <img src=\"https://www.strangerfoods.org/images/pulled-lamb-shawarma-sandwich.webp\" style=\"text-align:center;\"/>\n        <br>\n        <p style=\"font-family:sans-serif;>Slow-cooked lamb, piled into a warm pita with all the condiments you care for: this is the ultimate shawarma sandwich. Once cooked, the lamb keeps in the fridge so don\u2019t worry if there are fewer than eight of you for that first sandwich. The lamb is also great as a proper meal, rather than a sandwich, served as it is with a selection of sides: fattoush, butternut squash and a crisp green salad makes just one great combination.</p>",
      "image": "https://www.strangerfoods.org/images/pulled-lamb-shawarma-sandwich.webp",
      "date_published": "2026-07-25T00:00:00+00:00Z",
      "language": "en"
    },
    {
      "id": "https://www.strangerfoods.org/recipes/salmon-courgette-and-lemon-pasta-with-a-herby-dressing",
      "url": "https://www.strangerfoods.org/recipes/salmon-courgette-and-lemon-pasta-with-a-herby-dressing",
      "title": "Salmon, courgette and lemon pasta with a herby dressing",
      "content_html": "<h1 style=\"text-align:center;font-family:sans-serif;\">Salmon, courgette and lemon pasta with a herby dressing</h1>\n        <br>\n        <img src=\"https://www.strangerfoods.org/images/salmon-courgette-and-lemon-pasta-with-a-herby-dressing.webp\" style=\"text-align:center;\"/>\n        <br>\n        <p style=\"font-family:sans-serif;>This fresh and zingy creamy dressing, bursting with fresh herbs, yoghurt and plenty of black pepper, pairs perfectly with roasted salmon and charred courgettes. While fresh salmon is used here, tinned or smoked salmon are also great budget-friendly options.</p>",
      "image": "https://www.strangerfoods.org/images/salmon-courgette-and-lemon-pasta-with-a-herby-dressing.webp",
      "date_published": "2026-07-20T00:00:00+00:00Z",
      "language": "en"
    },
